---
layout: hub-app.njk
title: Wikidata query explanations
appBase: /web/hub/wikidata-explanations
appNoScript: true
appSource: https://github.com/danbri/factoidal-core/tree/main/docs/web/hub/wikidata-explanations
appEngineLabel: Wikidata result views
appEngineUrl: ../wikidata-results/
permalink: /web/hub/wikidata-explanations/index.html
---
{%- set ruleText = {
  "R-MULT-DUP": "identical rows can repeat",
  "R-GROUP-KEY-MULT": "an item appears once per value of a grouped column",
  "R-COUNT-ROWS": "the count counts rows, not distinct things",
  "R-GROUP-BY-LABEL": "different things with the same label are merged",
  "R-DIRECT-ONLY": "a place or part-of link is matched directly only",
  "R-COUNT-STMTS": "the count counts statements, not items",
  "R-REDIRECT-ID": "uses an item ID that is now a redirect",
  "R-JOIN-DROP": "values with no match silently disappear",
  "R-LIMIT-NOORDER": "LIMIT without ORDER BY: an arbitrary subset",
  "R-DELETED-ID": "uses a property or item that no longer exists",
  "R-SCOPE-LEAK": "a column can never have a value",
  "R-MINUS-NOSHARED": "an exclusion that removes nothing",
  "R-EXTERNAL": "results depend on an external service"
} -%}
<div class="wdx">
  <header class="intro">
    <h1>Wikidata query explanations</h1>
    <p>What each of Martin Poulter's {{ counts.total }} Wikidata queries asks for, stated precisely:
    which conditions apply, what is optional or excluded, and the ways the results can differ from
    what the title suggests. Each explanation describes the <strong>Factoidal rewrite</strong> of the
    query for the QLever endpoint.</p>
    <p>The explanations are generated by rules from the parsed query; no language model is used.
    Each statement names the rule that produced it, and each caveat is marked
    <em>changes_answer</em>, <em>scope</em> or <em>display</em>. They have not yet been reviewed by
    a person: treat them as a draft.</p>
    <p class="counts">{{ counts.explained }} explained ·
    {% for reason, n in counts.stubs %}{{ n }} {{ reason | replace("_", " ") }}{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    · generated {{ generated }} · <a href="explanations.json">data (JSON)</a></p>
  </header>

  <nav class="by-rule" aria-labelledby="by-rule-h">
    <h2 id="by-rule-h">Queries whose results may differ from their title</h2>
    <dl>
    {%- for group in byRule %}
      <dt>{{ ruleText[group.rule] or group.rule }} <code>{{ group.rule }}</code> ({{ group.ids | length }})</dt>
      <dd>{% for id in group.ids %}<a href="#{{ id }}">{{ id | replace("mlp-", "") }}</a>{% if not loop.last %} {% endif %}{% endfor %}</dd>
    {%- endfor %}
    </dl>
  </nav>

  {%- for q in queries %}
  <article class="query" id="{{ q.id }}">
    <header>
      <h2><a href="#{{ q.id }}">{{ q.id }}</a> {{ q.title | escape }}</h2>
      {%- if q.titleDirective %}<p class="directive">Query's own #title: {{ q.titleDirective | escape }}</p>{% endif %}
      {%- if q.section | length > 1 %}<p class="section">{{ q.section.slice(0, -1) | join(" › ") | escape }}</p>{% endif %}
      {%- if q.answerChanging | length %}
      <ul class="badges" aria-label="Caveats that change the answer">
        {%- for rule in q.answerChanging %}<li title="{{ ruleText[rule] or rule }}">{{ rule }}</li>{% endfor %}
      </ul>
      {%- endif %}
    </header>
    {%- if q.stub %}
    <p class="stub">Not explained:
      {%- if q.stub == "factoidal_parse_failed" %} the Factoidal parser does not yet accept this rewrite (a named subquery, <code>WITH … AS</code>).
      {%- elif q.stub == "skipped_unsupported" %} the query uses a service or feature that the QLever rewrite does not support, so there is no Factoidal rewrite.
      {%- elif q.stub == "parse_error" %} the original query could not be parsed.
      {%- else %} {{ q.stub }}.{% endif %}
      {%- if q.diagnostics | length %} ({{ q.diagnostics | join(", ") | escape }}){% endif %}</p>
    {%- else %}
    <pre class="explanation">{{ q.explanation | escape }}</pre>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if q.rewritten %}
    <details><summary>Factoidal rewrite (explained above)</summary><pre class="sparql"><code>{{ q.rewritten | escape }}</code></pre></details>
    {%- endif %}
    <details><summary>Original query</summary><pre class="sparql"><code>{{ q.original | escape }}</code></pre>
      <p class="links"><a href="https://query.wikidata.org/#{{ q.original | urlencode }}">Open the original in the Wikidata Query Service</a> · <a href="{{ q.source }}">Source page revision</a></p>
    </details>
  </article>
  {%- endfor %}

  <footer class="about">
    <h2>About this page</h2>
    <p>Parser: {{ parser }}. Wikidata labels and descriptions retrieved {{ labels.retrieved }} ({{ labels.license }}).
    Corpus <code>{{ corpus.corpus_sha256 | truncate(16, true, "…") }}</code>, Factoidal rewriter commit <code>{{ corpus.lean_git_commit | truncate(12, true, "") }}</code>.</p>
    <p>Queries: {{ corpus.attribution }}, from
    <a href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/User:MartinPoulter/queries">User:MartinPoulter/queries</a>
    and related pages, under <a href="{{ corpus.license_url }}">{{ corpus.license }}</a>;
    the explanations derived from them are shared under the same licence.</p>
  </footer>
</div>
